
SECTION A — the detector hook fires ONLY on explicit end-of-speech evidence
  [PASS] A1 — an interim never fires onTurnPending, and releases nothing
  [PASS] A2 — `is_final` WITHOUT `speech_final` never fires onTurnPending, even though the turn is later released by inference
  [PASS] A3 — a provider that reports NO endpoint claim (`isSpeechFinal` absent) never fires onTurnPending
  [PASS] A4 — `speech_final: true` on a finished thought fires onTurnPending ONCE, with the exact text later released
  [PASS] A5 — the standalone end-of-speech MARKER after an `is_final` chunk fires onTurnPending with the held text
  [PASS] A6 — the detector's own guards run FIRST: filler, hold phrase and an incomplete thought never fire it even with `speech_final`
  [PASS] A7 — new speech inside the window is seen as the fed segment; onTurnEnd then carries the merged text, not the announced one
  [PASS] A8 — a detector with no subscriber behaves byte-for-byte as before (hook is pure observation)

SECTION B — the pipeline speculates only on evidence, and never leaves a stray request behind
